## Submission

When you are done, submit your changes as a git patch. Follow these steps IN
ORDER, as SEPARATE commands:

Step 1 — create the patch, listing only the source files you modified:

```bash
cd {{ instance.repo_path }} && git diff -- path/to/file1 path/to/file2 > /tmp/patch.txt
```

Step 2 — verify the patch only contains your intended source changes (headers
show `--- a/` and `+++ b/`):

```bash
cat /tmp/patch.txt
```

Step 3 — submit with this EXACT command (single command, must exit 0):

```bash
echo COMPLETE_TASK_AND_SUBMIT_FINAL_OUTPUT && cat /tmp/patch.txt
```

The marker `COMPLETE_TASK_AND_SUBMIT_FINAL_OUTPUT` MUST be the first line of the
command output; everything after it is treated as your final patch. If the
command fails (non-zero exit status) nothing is submitted. After submitting you
cannot continue working on this task.
